# Skeletal mesh asset names

A skeletal mesh is `SM_` plus the asset name in Pascal case.

- `knight` becomes `SM_Knight`.
- `barbarian` becomes `SM_Barbarian`.
- `mage` becomes `SM_Mage`.
- `ranger` becomes `SM_Ranger`.

Do not append a number when another asset already uses the bare name. The mesh is `SM_Knight`. The material can keep the name `knight`.

The package name and the object name are the same: `SM_Knight.SM_Knight`.

Rename the mesh in the Content Browser. That writes a redirector. Then right-click the folder and run Update Redirector References. Do not add an `ObjectRedirect` to `Config/DefaultEngine.ini`.
